Template: drumee-infra/description
Type: string
Default: My Great Drumee Team
Description: Please enter a label for this Drumee instance
 A human-friendly name for your team or instance.

Template: drumee-infra/domain
Type: string
Default: example.com
Description: Please enter the domain name
 This is the domain name your Drumee instance will use.

Template: drumee-infra/local_mode
Type: boolean
Default: true
Description: Please confirm only local network
 You have provided "local" as domain name. That means your Drumee instance
 won't be reachable from the public Internet.

Template: drumee-infra/service
Type: string
Description: Please enter the list of services to enable
 Comma-separated list of optional services to enable for this instance.

Template: drumee-infra/ip4
Type: select
Choices: ${__IP4_LIST__}, other
Default: other
Description: Please select your server IPv4 address
 If you set a private address, your Drumee won't be reachable from the public Internet.

Template: drumee-infra/public_ip4
Type: string
Description: Please enter your server IPv4 address
 If you set a private address, your Drumee won't be reachable from the public Internet.

Template: drumee-infra/ip6
Type: select
Choices: ${__IP6_LIST__}, other
Default: other
Description: Please select your server IPv6 address
 If you select a private address, your Drumee won't be reachable from the public Internet.

Template: drumee-infra/public_ip6
Type: string
Description: Please enter your server IPv6 address
 If you set a private address, your Drumee won't be reachable from the public Internet.

Template: drumee-infra/admin_email
Type: string
Default: admin@example.com
Description: Please enter the administrator email
 This address is used as the administrator login identifier and to send
 technical notifications to.

Template: drumee-infra/acme_email
Type: string
Default:
Description: Please enter the ACME email account
 If you are not using your own SSL certificates, Drumee uses ZeroSSL to
 automatically issue your SSL certificates. This email is provided to
 zerossl.com as the account identifier.

Template: drumee-infra/db_dir
Type: string
Default: /srv/db
Description: Please enter the path to your Drumee database
 This storage area must not be shared with another application or a native
 system path such as /usr, /sys, ...

Template: drumee-infra/data_dir
Type: string
Default: /data
Description: Please enter the path to your Drumee filesystem storage
 This storage area must not be shared with another application or a native
 system path such as /usr, /sys, ...

Template: drumee-infra/backup_location
Type: string
Description: Please enter the location of your Drumee backup
 It should be located on a different partition from the data storage.
 For example /my-backup or remote.server.backup:/my-backup.

Template: drumee-infra/exchange_location
Type: string
Default: /exchangearea
Description: Please enter the location of your exchange area
 A directory to transfer files between the host filesystem and the Drumee
 filesystem. It must not be shared with a native system path such as /usr, /sys, ...

Template: drumee-infra/own_ssl
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Do you have your own SSL certificates?
 If not, Drumee uses ZeroSSL to automatically issue your SSL certificates.

Template: drumee-infra/own_ssl_path
Type: string
Description: Please enter the location of your SSL certificates
 Certificates must be wildcard and cover every name Drumee serves:
 example.com, *.example.com, jit.example.com, *.jit.example.com,
 vendors.example.com and *.vendors.example.com.
 .
 Each subdomain needs its own wildcard entry: a wildcard matches a single label,
 so *.example.com does NOT cover anything below vendors.example.com.
